H7725","Hc/Vhw3ms","and he restored"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["עָרֵי","'arei","H5892","HNcmpc","[the] cities of"],["יִשְׂרָאֵל","yisra'el","H3478","HNpl","Israel"]],"x":[[12013018,12013019,5],[12010032,12010032,3]],"xn":2}},"people":[{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[1,10,12]},{"id":"jehu_817","name":"Jehu","also":"","summary":"King of Israel, the son of Jehoshaphat (2 Kings 9:2), and grandson of Nimshi. The story of his exaltation to the throne is deeply interesting.","verses":47,"father":"Jehoshaphat","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"ahaziah_121","name":"Ahaziah","also":"Jehoahaz, Azariah","summary":"The son of Joram, or Jehoram, and sixth king of Judah. Called Jehoahaz (2 Chr. 21:17; 25:23), and Azariah (2 Chr. 22:6). Guided by his idolatrous mother Athaliah, his reign was disastrous (2 Kings 8:24-29; 9:29).","verses":26,"father":"Jehoram","mother":"Athaliah","v":[1]},{"id":"joash_1632","name":"Joash","also":"Jehoash","summary":"The son of King Ahaziah. While yet an infant, he was saved from the general massacre of the family by his aunt Jehosheba, and was apparently the only surviving descendant of Solomon (2 Chr. 21:4, 17).","verses":19,"father":"Ahaziah","mother":"Zibiah","v":[1]},{"id":"jehoahaz_784","name":"Jehoahaz","also":"","summary":"The son and successor of Jehu, king of Israel (2 Kings 10:35). He reigned seventeen years, and followed the evil ways of the house of Jeroboam.","verses":14,"father":"Jehu","mother":"","v":[1,4,7,8,9,10,22,25]},{"id":"jeroboam_872","name":"Jeroboam","also":"","summary":"The son of Nebat (1 Kings 11:26-39), “an Ephrathite,” the first king of the ten tribes, over whom he reigned twenty-two years (B.C. 976-945).","verses":81,"father":"Nebat","mother":"Zeruah","v":[2,6,11]},{"id":"nebat_2165","name":"Nebat","also":"","summary":"Sight; aspect, the father of Jeroboam, the king of Israel (1 Kings 11:26, etc.).","verses":25,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2,11]},{"id":"hazael_1463","name":"Hazael","also":"","summary":"Whom God beholds, an officer of Ben-hadad II., king of Syria, who ultimately came to the throne, according to the word of the Lord to Elijah (1 Kings 19:15), after he had put the king to death (2 Kings 8:15).","verses":21,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3,22,24,25]},{"id":"ben-hadad_454","name":"Ben-hadad","also":"","summary":"King of Damascus, and successor of his father Hazael on the throne of Syria (2 Kings 13:3, 4).","verses":4,"father":"Hazael","mother":"","v":[3,24,25]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[5,23]},{"id":"joash_1633","name":"Joash","also":"Jehoash","summary":"The son and successor of Jehoahaz, king of Israel (2 Kings 14:1; comp. 12:1; 13:10). When he ascended the throne the kingdom was suffering from the invasion of the Syrians.","verses":23,"father":"Jehoahaz","mother":"","v":[9,10,12,13,14,25]},{"id":"amaziah_214","name":"Amaziah","also":"","summary":"The son and successor of Joash, and eighth king of the separate kingdom of Judah (2 Kings 14:1-4). He began his reign by punishing the murderers of his father (5-7; 2 Chr. 25:3-5).","verses":34,"father":"Joash","mother":"Jehoaddan","v":[12]},{"id":"jeroboam_873","name":"Jeroboam","also":"","summary":"Jeroboam II., the son and successor of Jehoash, and the fourteenth king of Israel, over which he ruled for forty-one years, B.C. 825-784 (2 Kings 14:23).","verses":14,"father":"Joash","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"elisha_1153","name":"Elisha","also":"Eliseus","summary":"God his salvation, the son of Shaphat of Abel-meholah, who became the attendant and disciple of Elijah (1 Kings 19:16-19). His name first occurs in the command given to Elijah to anoint him as his successor (1 Kings 19:16).","verses":53,"father":"Shaphat","mother":"","v":[14,15,16,17,20,21]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[23]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[23]}],"places":[{"id":"samaria_1022","name":"Samaria","kind":"Region","lat":32.33142,"lon":35.22859,"summary":"A watch-mountain or a watch-tower. In the heart of the mountains of Israel, a few miles north-west of Shechem, stands the “hill of Shomeron,” a solitary mountain, a great “mamelon.”","verses":114,"v":[1,6,9,10,13]},{"id":"syria_1122","name":"Syria","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":37.5,"lon":37.5,"summary":"(Heb. Aram), the name in the Old Testament given to the whole country which lay to the north-east of Phoenicia, extending to beyond the Euphrates and the Tigris.","verses":64,"v":[3,4,7,17,19,22,24]},{"id":"aphek_73","name":"Aphek","kind":"City","lat":32.77827,"lon":35.69875,"summary":"A town on the road from Damascus to Palestine, in the level plain east of Jordan, near which Benhadad was defeated by the Israelites (1 Kings 20:26, 30; 2 Kings 13:17).","verses":3,"v":[17]}],"events":[{"id":"reign_of_jehoahaz_195","title":"Reign of Jehoahaz","year":-857,"summary":"Passage: 2 Kings 13:1–9. People: Jehoahaz. Place: Samaria. Lasted about 17 years.","v":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9]},{"id":"death_of_jehoahaz_196","title":"Death of Jehoahaz","year":-840,"summary":"Passage: 2 Kings 13:9. People: Jehoahaz. Place: Samaria.","v":[9]},{"id":"reign_of_jehoash_197","title":"Reign of Jehoash","year":-840,"summary":"Passage: 2 Kings 13:10–13. People: Joash. Place: Samaria. Lasted about 16 years.","v":[10,11,12,13]},{"id":"death_of_jehoahash_201","title":"Death of Jehoahash","year":-825,"summary":"Passage: 2 Kings 13:13. People: Joash. Place: Samaria.","v":[13]},{"id":"prophecies_of_elisha_186","title":"Prophecies of Elisha","year":-897,"summary":"Passage: 2 Kings 2:15–13:21. People: Elisha. Lasted about 59 years.","v":[14,15,16,17,18,19,20,21]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[6242,6242,6242,8141,4428,4428,4428,3101,3101,1121,274,274,3063,3063,3059,1121,3058,3058,4427,4427,5921,3478,8111,8111,8111,8111,8111,7651,8141],[6213,6213,6213,7451,5869,5869,5869,3068,3068,3068,1980,1980,2403,2403,834,3379,1121,5028,5028,3478,3478,3478,2398,2398,3808,3808,3808,5493,5493,4480,4480],[639,639,639,3068,3068,3068,2734,3478,3478,5414,5414,5414,5414,3605,3027,3027,3027,2371,2371,4428,758,758,2371,2371,1121,1130],[3059,3059,2470,6440,6440,3068,3068,3068,3068,3068,3068,8085,413,413,3588,7200,7200,3906,3906,4428,4428,4428,758,758,3905,3905,3478,3478],[3068,3068,3068,5414,3478,3467,3467,3318,3318,3318,3027,3027,758,758,758,1121,1121,1121,3478,3478,3427,168,168,168,168,8543,8543,8543,8543],[389,3808,3808,3808,5493,5493,2403,2403,2403,834,1004,1004,3379,3379,3478,3478,3478,2398,2398,1980,1980,1980,1980,1980,1980,1980,842,842,842,1571,5975,5975,8111,8111],[3059,3808,3808,5971,7604,3588,2572,6571,6235,7393,6235,6235,505,7273,7273,3588,4428,4428,758,758,6,6,6,7760,7760,7760,6083,6083,6083,1758,1758],[3499,3499,3499,3499,1697,1697,1697,3059,3059,3605,3605,3605,834,834,1369,1369,1369,3789,3789,3789,3789,5921,5612,5612,1697,1697,1697,4428,4428,4428,3478,3478],[3059,3059,7901,5973,1,1,6912,6912,6912,8111,8111,1121,1121,1121,3101,4427,8478,8478,8478],[7970,7970,7970,8141,4428,4428,4428,3101,3101,3063,3063,3060,1121,3059,3059,4427,4427,5921,3478,8111,8111,8337,8337,8337,8337,8141],[6213,6213,6213,7451,5869,5869,586